        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mia Hansen-Løve, Isabelle Huppert, Marc Rothemund, Fred Breinersdorfer\n- Films: Things to Come, Goodbye First Love, Sophie Scholl – The Final Days\n- Events: 66th Berlin International Film Festival, 78th Academy Awards\n- Awards: Silver Bear for Best Director, Best Foreign Language Film nomination\n- Roles: director, writer, actress, philosophy professor\n\nFacts:\n- In 2005, Marc Rothemund directed Sophie Scholl – The Final Days, which was written by Fred Breinersdorfer.\n- In 2005, Sophie Scholl – The Final Days received numerous awards, including the Silver Bear for Best Director at the Berlin International Film Festival.\n- Sophie Scholl – The Final Days was nominated for the 78th Academy Awards for Best Foreign Language Film.\n- In 2011, Goodbye First Love (French: Un amour de jeunesse) was released as a Franco-German film directed by Mia Hansen-Løve.\n- In 2016, Mia Hansen-Løve won the Silver Bear for Best Director for Things to Come at the 66th Berlin International Film Festival.\n- Things to Come is a 2016 film starring Isabelle Huppert as middle-aged philosophy professor Nathalie Chazeaux, whose life is undergoing a series of separations.",
